 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186175923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186175924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1031 "Finding Equations of Perpendicular Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1033 3562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1034 1.1558263047756883 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050473 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "4c6d2580-78c9-5782-9c3a-465dcd055b32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1031 "Equations of Lines in Point-Slope Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1033 418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050635 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5a901d31-08d1-5602-a6b3-9ae8fa80845b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064259 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line Using Differentiation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1033 332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1034 0.9795434122769167 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050711 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "608cf86b-83ea-5cc3-a6a8-222e7fa44e21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186166879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1031 "Finding Derivatives Using a Graphing Calculator" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1033 3172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050960 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "75a5f951-7177-5324-a4da-1191c703ae8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091953 #edb/ref 1069 "e-148" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091953 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the slope of the normal line to the curve $y = 2x^3 -x^2$ at the point $(1,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4a734f55-ceac-587c-a831-fa8bed578a99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091953 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x) = 2x^3-x^2.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\nf'(x)  =6x^2 -2x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = 6(1)^2 - 2(1) = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line $m'$ is\n\n$$\nm' = -\\dfrac{1}{m} = -\\dfrac 1 4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091954 #edb/ref 1069 "e-149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091954 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $f(x) = 2\\sqrt{x} -4x$ at the point $(1,-2)$ intersects the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091954 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df59a07a-922c-50b9-8c2c-22ed57ac2bda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186091954 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}-4x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{1/2}-4x) \\\\  & ={x}^{-1/2}-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1) = (1)^{-1/2} - 4 = -3,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm' = -\\dfrac{1}{m} = \\dfrac 1 3.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(-2) & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y+2 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{1}{3}-2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{7}{3} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x & =\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(7,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092083 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6080" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092083 #edb/ref 1071 "The equation of the normal line to the curve $y=x^3 - x^2$ at the point $(1,0)$ is given by $y=px+q$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. Find the values of $p$ and $q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092083 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e405bf60-d500-55df-90be-a938dc9dfc93" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092083 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)=x^3 - x^2.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-{x}^{2})=3{x}^{2}-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1, 0){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=3-2=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line $m'$ is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\dfrac{1}{m}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =-(x-1) \\\\ y & =-x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-1$ and $q=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092240 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092240 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092240 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186092724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218609