,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(25)}=- \\frac{1}{25}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(15)&=- \\frac{1}{25}(x-(1))\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x-(- \\frac{1}{25})+(15)\\\\y&=- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{1}{25}x+\\frac{376}{25}&=0\\\\x&=376.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(376,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493309 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493319 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{20}{x}+10$ at the point $(1,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c1268dd-9a0b-5590-983e-596506fe3286" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493318 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(\\frac{20}{x}+10)\\\\&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(10 + \\frac{20}{x})\\\\&=-20x^{-2}\\\\&=- \\frac{20}{x^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(1)=-20=-20,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-20)}=\\frac{1}{20}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{20}(x-(1))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x-(\\frac{1}{20})+(30)\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20}x+\\frac{599}{20}&=0\\\\x&=-599.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the  $x$-axis at $(-599,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493315 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493323 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30$ at the point $(0,30)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe normal line intersects the $x$-axis at\n$($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}} $).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3c9763c-f1e1-51a2-887f-38a4a610161d" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493321 #edb/ref 1074 "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(18 x^{2} - 36 x + 30)=36 x - 36.\n$$\n\nSo the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\nm=f'(0)=-36=-36,\n$$\n\nand therefore the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=-\\frac{1}{(-36)}=\\frac{1}{36}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(30)&=\\frac{1}{36}(x-(0))\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{36}x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we find the point of intersection with the $x$-axis by setting $y=0$ and solving the resulting equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{36}x+30&=0\\\\\\frac{1}{36}x&=-30\\\\x&=-1080.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the normal line intersects the $x$-axis at $(-1080,0).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092385.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493324 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "6f93f05c-93ce-5432-b4e0-7ec958ee8e90" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186092240.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186493326 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "733357e0-41a3-5401-bdd5-4100649b68a2" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186523281 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523281 #edb/ref 108